A||||12||Gold-86SE||No dome light, SES, or door chime - need help badly.||||1||
Z||000000||Gold-86SE||05-12-2001||04:40 PM||||<BR>Ok guys, this is weird and is throwing me for a loop.<P>I have a working horn, turn signals flash, oil indicator light (illuminates when turn on key).  Also, I don't have dome lights, nor a door chime (when the door is open), nor do I get an SES light to check codes.<P>The strange thing is that all the light bulbs (dome and dash) are fine, all have the filaments (read no burnt bulbs).<P>Another strange thing is that if I turn on the flashers, externally they flash, but on the instrument cluster the signals themselves not illuminate instead the high beam indicator flashes and the fuel gauge ticks backward toward E, until it reaches empty.<P>I have checked the fuses are all the proper amp and none were blown.<P>Talk about electrical gremlines, this one appears to have them. What do I do?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||05-12-2001||06:06 PM||||<BR>As for the dome lights, I figured out what their problem was.  No fuse.  According to chilton, it was not needed, but apparantly the number 17 fuse, bottom right, is necessary for dome lights.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||05-12-2001||06:07 PM||||<BR>The blue diggy thingy. Does it have to be out of an 87 for it to work on an 87?  I tried one out of an 84 and an 86 neither work. Suffice it to say the blue diggy thingy is missing on the 87.  Do I a blue diggy thing for the SES light to work?||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||05-12-2001||08:37 PM||||So the blue dingy thing-I think you are talking about the turn signal flasher.  Your signals work normally other than indicators don't flash on dash.  And your SES light does not illuminate with the engine off, ignition in run position. correct.  first I would check that your dash/cluster is plugged in securely.  Check your grounds for the cluster.  It has been found that a bad ECM can be a cause for no SES light.  sounds to me like you have more than one problem. ??||||reg||1
Z||000004||drednot||05-12-2001||08:52 PM||||fieros have door chimes???  This is news to me.  mine sure dosent.||||reg||1
Z||000005||PBJ||05-12-2001||09:06 PM||||my 86 has key, headlight and my wife says it even chims for seat belt not buckled.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Indiana_resto_guy||05-12-2001||10:06 PM||||Sounds like a fuse link to me.<BR>Check the ones out at the junction block in the engine bay.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Gold-86SE||05-13-2001||09:46 AM||||<BR>Allow me to update.<P>As my second post states, I determined the problem with the dome lights, but here is the real kicker.  I was curious to see (even though I had done this earlier and no SES light flashed) if the SES might flash at me.<P>So, removed the ciggy cover plate and jumped the connector on the aldl to retrieve the codes. Guess what happens?  The radiator fans turns on. Yep you got it the radiator fan, the last thing that should be happening, and still no SES light.<P>Well, I am thinking that the problem lies in this: The Fiero has an aftermarket stereo and I think someone missed wired the unit.  Guess, I'll have to pull to find out.<P>If I find it, I'll let you know.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Vader||05-13-2001||12:57 PM||||Check the base connectors at the side of the instrument cluster.  All IP functions are routed through these connectors, and the SES lamp is one of those functions, as well as the turn/hazard indicator lamps, gauges, etc.  <BR>Make sure the grounds are intact as well.<P>------------------<BR>"<I>Make Me Bad</I>"||||reg||1
Z||000009||mbramble||05-13-2001||02:00 PM||||I believe -- though my son has my car so I can't confirm it right this minute -- that when you turn the key to ON with the ALDL test pins shorted, that the fan does come on.  I am pretty sure I remember that happening the last time I did it, and wondering why that might be.<P>According to my 85 Service Manual, if the ECM light doesn't come on and the engine runs OK, check:<BR>- faulty light bulb<BR>- circuit 419 open. This is the line from the ECM that provides a ground to the Check Engine light to turn it on. It comes in on pin 10 of connector C206 (the one on the right side of the instrument panel) on a brn/wht wire. <BR>- guage fuse blown which would also result in no ajar light, e-brake light, temp warning light, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000010||mbramble||05-13-2001||02:28 PM||||My son just came in from church and we went out and checked -- when you put the ignition switch to ON with the test pins shorted, the fan does come on....||||reg||1
Z||000011||Gold-86SE||05-13-2001||10:33 PM||||<BR>mbramble, that was some of the best advice. fortunately, no one had done anything drastic to the vehicle.<P>The problem was a half-plugged in plug on the right side of the instrument cluster.  Plugged that thing in all the way and everything worked great.  man that was great. joy joy happy happy.<P>thanks guys||||reg||1
Z||000012||mbramble||05-13-2001||10:38 PM||||That would be a good reason for flakey problems!! Congrats...<P>||||reg||1
